  "summary": {
    "en": "Communal clashes in Lakes state, especially around Rumbek, have intensified with curfews imposed and caretaker governor Rin Tueny returning to address the violence. UNMISS has increased civilian protection efforts after deadly attacks in Rumbek, while SSPDF soldiers were wounded in an assault on a Mundri West military outpost and the U.S. Embassy condemned an assault on WFP workers in Jonglei that involved looting of aid. An AIC cleric was shot dead in Juba and a Juba High Court sentenced five officers to 24 years for raiding a general's home. The lethal communal violence now far exceeds the two battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.",
